{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/977962-willpower-conversion","id":977962,"title":"Willpower conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T14:06:49-07:00","id":977962,"title":"Willpower conversion","content":"Willpower is a somewhat untapped/untargeted resource, as far as i can tell. One would have thought that draining an opponents mental reservoir, refreshing one's own and performing the mental equivalent of the hearts blood rote to fuel pattern magic with raw willlower would be a trope in play. <br /> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that a Mind/Prime effect ought to be able to convert willpower to quintessence and vice versa, even if the product were or needed to be vibrantly resonant with the caster's essence. HDYDT seems to indicate that mind/forces fuels pattern magic with strong emotions/will. <br /> <br /> <br /> The economy of this escapes me though; given 1Q can be used to reduce a casting TN and 1WP can be used for a *success*, i would presume that WP has a heavier game &quot;weight&quot; than Q does. I toyed with the conversion ratio being 1WP=2Q but if feels a little off. Also, Mind/Prime magi would have an immense advantage over others in pure battery terms. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone have any suggestions for that or for spheres levels for personal/other targeted psychic leech/bolster shenanigans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12052-chax2k","name":"Chax2k","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:29:52-07:00","id":977971,"title":"","content":"I think a Mind/Prime effect for converting WP into Quint makes sense. 1Q for 1WP would be the easiest way to do it. But if you don't think that's enough to warrant the expenditure, you could try to go for 2Q for 1WP.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could make it so Permanent WP points can be exchanged for a large amount of Quint, not unlike how lethal damage gives more than bashing damage.<br /> Since WP is the easiest thing to level up, the cost would be big, but not devastating if the need for Quint was just that great.<br /> <br /> Actual, thinking about it, perhaps Mind and Prime could also draw Quint out of your very memories, converting Experience into Quintessence. You'd definitely need Mind 3 for yourself or Mind 4 for others though, along with Prime 3.<br /> <br /> The amount of Quint one would get from experience would probably depend on how generous the ST is at giving out exp.<br /> Taken to the extreme, you could turn full long term memories into Quint, and then lose certain abilities. Maybe even forget details like your name or your childhood. The Quint would be great, but the loss would be inconsolable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T14:33:48-07:00","id":977973,"title":"","content":"I both like and dislike your idea.<br /> <br /> I like it because it seems coherent. You can find Quintessence in Life, Matter and Force patterns, why could you not find it in Mind forms ! Though, I will keep it to 1WP=1Q. I would even tend to do the contrary and go for 2WP=1Q. Quintessence does not only lower the difficulty of magick, it is used to fuel magick (create new patterns, affect patterns directly, create wonders, ...). Basically, quintessence is the more expensive ressource of Mages. But 1WP for 1Q could be enough. I mean, you have pretty much this conversion when you disrupt life patterns to get Quintessence.<br /> <br /> However :<br /> - There are no such things as Mind patterns if I do not mistake. Mind 5 is enough (and necessary) to create new Mind forms (correct me if I'm wrong). I'm not sure you can destroy Mind forms to get Quintessence since they are not really Patterns. But it could function nonetheless. In the end, everything is quintessence. Hermetics would say that Mind is there to design patterns so... basically Mind is source of all patterns (in that paradigm at least).<br /> - And story-wise, you would get a lot of Jhor out of that (same as human sacrifice I woud say). Nasty thing... Plus, it would have to be ok with your paradigm and you would have to find a reason for your Mage to believe in that kind of practice. Not possible in all paradigms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:52:45-07:00","id":978013,"title":"","content":"I see your point about mind patterns not being a thing, just as time has no pattern magic analogue (though the temptation to try time3/prime2 to literally spin more time into a scene and make a slow time bubble on the cheap) i'd perhaps been lead astray by thoughts of emotion powering effects and recalled Rage as a quintessentially potent emotional resource. <br /> <br /> What then is willpower? Permanent WP might be the founding strength and capacity of the human soul (or an artifact thereof), and temp WP a representation of it's degree of ordered thought (entropy?) that depletes as you apply it, reordered by nature fulfilment or rest. In which case mind/entropy could be used to unmuddle a tired ego? <br /> <br /> I had also hoped to propose such futher amusements as <br /> <br /> Willpower periapts (mind/prime/matter stash WP for later use) <br /> Borrowing against your future Will (mind/time to steal future rested WP refresh. Or someone else's)<br /> Depressing a target into uselesness (mind/entropy to &quot;destroy&quot; temp WP )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12052-chax2k","name":"Chax2k","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T16:22:08-07:00","id":978025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/977962-willpower-conversion?p=977973#post977973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no such things as Mind patterns if I do not mistake. Mind 5 is enough (and necessary) to create new Mind forms (correct me if I'm wrong). I'm not sure you can destroy Mind forms to get Quintessence since they are not really Patterns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely true. I remember the Revised core book under the Prime sphere saying that you could mix Prime 3 with Mind in order to take the Quintessence out of Mind pattern tass, such as dreams or memories. Heck, the Maya is to Mind what Spirit is to the Umbra. So if Spirit patterns are a thing because of the umbra, then by the same token Mind patterns are a thing.<br /> <br /> Also, couldn't Resonance be considered a form of Mind pattern? You need mind magic to sense it, and you can't really change strong resonance without Mind magic, how is that any different from the other pattern spheres?<br /> <br /> Actually, I'd make the argument that all spheres have associated patterns to them, each at various tiers of separation from the mundane world.<br /> <br /> The way I've seen it, the nine spheres fit into three tiers.<br /> <br /> At the base tier are the three Material patterns. Matter, Forces, and Life. All of which comprise everything that we can physically see and interact with mundanely. What more is there to say? Sleepers are the most familiar with this stuff.<br /> <br /> In the middle tier are the three Primordial patterns. Spirit, Entropy, and Mind. These are a step removed from material reality, but still be sensed and manipulated by mundane will. Be it by being sensitive to spiritual activity, empathetic towards emotions, or simply aware of ones fate and good at statistics. In addition, while Matter, Forces, and Life make up the building blocks for all physical things in mundane reality. Spirit, Entropy, and Mind make up the building blocks of the near umbra. Entropy of the Lower Umbra, Spirit of the Middle Umbra, and Mind of the High Umbra. As a result, Sleepers may be aware of these forces and aware of many philosophical and mystical debates about them, they may even feel sympathetic towards them or feel a personal connection to heavy resonance locations, their own fate and eventual decay, and even a vague sense of where or when the gauntlet weakens. They may not understand these patterns, but they can still feel them for what they are, even if they later dismiss them.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there's the outer tier which holds the three Esoteric patterns. Corr. Time, and Prime. These patterns are both an integral part of mundane reality, but at the same time lie completely outside our ability to manipulate or even sense them mundanely. Sleepers are trapped with the core belief built in us that space is big and distance is not an illusion. Time too functions exactly how we perceive it, as a constant forward march. While Prime lies completely outside of anything anyone but the awakened can even comprehend. Sleepers simply don't consider Space and Time to be related to one another. Sure, they may hear all sorts of Physics stuff that shows they are, but do they really understand it? If they did, they are more likely to be Extraordinary Citizens than simple sleepers. The same goes doubly for Prime, the very idea that these is this metaphysical substance, as the Technocracts may call it, Dark Matter, or Dark Energy, which binds everything together and simultaneously allows all fundamental things to function. Completely beyond their capability to understand. Even if they know of it, to understand it is a completely different enterprise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-28-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}